      "mergeID": "6a4bc134207a0a1242a8cf18",
      "mergedPostDetails": "In desktop mode, in any world, if you look around my moving your mouse fast-ish, the framerate can drop massively. It only happens while moving the mouse.\n\n1kHz polling rate, This only lags the game, not other applications.\n\nCPU (or individual thread) and GPU usage doesn't increase while moving the mouse, in fact it seems to drop while the lag spike is happening.\n\nie.: staying still: 200fps, ~ 50% cpu, 50% gpu\n\nlooking around at speed: ~50fps (depending on speed), ~30% cpu, 15% gpu\n\n(overall system usage)\n\nNo individual cpu core gets even remotely maxed out, didn't happen in earlier stable versions.\n\nSimilar in feel and probably causality to this issue: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1865-lag-spike-while-moving-the-mouse-with-the-menu-open\n\nTho, the lagspike isn't as massive as that, it's still noticeable. It reduces your framerate while moving the mouse to ~25% of the original framerate.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1865] Looking around with a mouse causes lag.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a3c271df744a3cbd7603107",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wonder if this bug is even Unity 6 specific. As far as I understand it, it can occur on Unity 2022.3.22f1 and becomes especially worse with the avatar debug menu open and/or on avatars with lots of physbone parameters (any parameter values updating frequently in general - velocities from looking around / moving are one of these).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
