      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This doesn't seem VRChat-specific as I've had this happen on many different games and on multiple PCs, the only real \"solution\" is to configure your mouse to lower its polling rate outside of games.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a3fc72d56d8704aacb989f3",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "5fd10fd5ca7a697fb6db2c93",
        "alias": "Gray Lizard",
        "aliasID": "65c8dad9ed6eefce4c5da381",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/7ad404754616d1c0eeeaae1e33dccea7.png",
        "created": "2020-12-09T17:56:37.689Z",
        "name": "Lenr",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-06-27T12:50:53.419Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a3c271df744a3cbd7603107",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Doesn't just happen in the menu, it just has a more noticeable effect there.\n\nHappens when just looking around fast in a world, but it's just less of an effect (but still quite annoying! I tried those surfing worlds, and it just wasn't viable like this.)\n\nSeems to happen even at lower polling rates too, it just has less of an effect.\n\nI set my polling rate down to 125Hz and it still had a noticeable effect while moving it around fast.\n\nBoth with the menu open, and just in the world looking around.\n\nStill tied to polling rate, as reducing it from 1kHz to 125Hz reduced the effect.\n\nSo:\n\n- 1kHz: 200fps regular, 10fps while moving the mouse in the menu fast\n\n- 125Hz: 200fps regular, 150fps while moving the mouse in the menu fast (around the same speed as i did on 1kHz setting)\n\nIt's even less noticeable while just looking around in a world fast, but it's still there.\n\nAnd setting it to 500Hz the effect becomes more noticeable, even tho i wouldn't consider this a high polling rate.\n\n(In fact 1kHz should be seen as a standard polling rate tbh, seeing as we nowadays have mice capable of 4kHz or 8kHz rates too.)\n\nSo setting your mouse to a lower polling rate isn't really an actual solution, it just reduces the effect, but the problem is still there.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
